WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.530
Oh, hello, hello.
噢，你好，你好。

9
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.170
I have an incentive for you.
我有个激励你的点子。

10
00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:33.650
Oh, do you?
噢，是吗？

11
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:45.790
If this becomes our most listened-to office ladies of all time, would you be willing to get an office ladies tattoo on your rear end?
如果这一集成为我们有史以来收听率最高的节目，你愿意在你的屁股上纹一个《办公室》女士的纹身吗？

12
00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:46.690
Me?
我？

13
00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:48.530
Both of us.
我们俩都纹。

14
00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.710
Matching office ladies tattoos on our tushes.
在我们的屁股上纹上配套的《办公室》女士纹身。

15
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.590
On the old SS Bernard?
纹在老屁股上？

16
00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.390
It's a no for me.
我拒绝。

17
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:02.510
I hope everyone will listen to this, but I'm not going to get a tattoo.
我希望大家都会收听这期节目，但我不会去纹身。

18
00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.870
Well, I've never gotten a tattoo.
嗯，我从来没纹过身。

19
00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:10.070
So I feel like the very first one maybe shouldn't be, like, where you work.
所以我感觉人生第一个纹身，或许不该是关于你工作的地方。

20
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:10.990
I don't know.
我不知道。

21
00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:11.730
I agree.
我同意。

22
00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:12.470
Right?
对吧？

23
00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:16.490
It's like, you know, if you work at Walmart, are you going to put Walmart on your butt?
就像，你知道，如果你在沃尔玛工作，你会把沃尔玛纹在屁股上吗？

24
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.990
Like, we work for office ladies.
毕竟我们为《办公室》女士工作。

25
00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.050
I know.
我知道。

26
00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:19.870
I know.
我知道。

27
00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.550
It would be a really intense form of advertising.
那将是一种非常硬核的广告形式。

28
00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:23.970
For who?
给谁看？

29
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:24.530
For who?
给谁看？

30
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:25.310
For who?
给谁看？

31
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.150
Just for Lee and Josh.
就给李和乔什看。

32
00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:34.090
For when we start wearing those thong bathing suits that we've always wanted to wear, Jenna.
为了当我们开始穿那些我们一直想穿的丁字泳装时，珍娜。

33
00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:38.590
We've always wanted to wear, you know, the bathing suits where your ass is falling out.
我们一直想穿那种，你知道的，屁股都露出来的泳装。

34
00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.850
You know I love a thong in any form.
你知道我喜欢任何形式的丁字裤。

35
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:41.910
Oh, you love that.
噢，你确实喜欢。

36
00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.510
You love a little string there.
你喜欢那儿有一根细带子。

37
00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.950
What are we doing?
我们在干嘛呢？

38
00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:45.410
Okay.
好吧。

39
00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:46.130
I don't know.
我不知道。

40
00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.010
Guys, today we're going to talk about The Incentive.
伙计们，今天我们要聊的是《激励》这一集。

41
00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:51.110
It is Season 8, Episode 2.
这是第八季第二集。

42
00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:55.770
It was written by Paul Lieberstein and directed by Charles McDougal.
由保罗·李伯斯坦编剧，查尔斯·麦克道格执导。

43
00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.770
Here is your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

44
00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:04.050
Robert California tells Andy he wants the Scranton branch to double their sales.
罗伯特·加州告诉安迪，他希望斯克兰顿分公司能将销售额翻倍。

45
00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:12.430
So Andy introduces a Points for Prizes reward program to incentivize these doubling of sales,
于是安迪推出了一个“积分换奖品”的奖励计划来激励大家实现销售翻倍，

46
00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:15.330
but it kind of soon blows up in his face.
但很快这事儿就让他自食其果了。

47
00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:19.650
Meanwhile, Pam and Angela become pregnant walking buddies.
与此同时，帕姆和安吉拉成了怀孕期间的步行搭子。

48
00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:21.550
So short-lived.
真是太短暂了。

49
00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.850
Like the shortest walking buddies ever.
简直是有史以来最短命的步行搭子。

50
00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:32.830
Fast fact number one is all about the making of the Saber Pyramid.
第一个冷知识是关于“赛博金字塔”的制作过程。

51
00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:41.170
Dwight is going to introduce this new electronic tablet in the shape of a pyramid that Saber wants them to sell.
德怀特要介绍这款Saber公司想让他们销售的、金字塔形状的新型电子平板电脑。

52
00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.730
It is very large and it doesn't do much.
它非常大，而且功能不多。

53
00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:49.690
Well, you know, Jenna, without the battery or optional memory booster, it's barely three pounds.
嗯，你知道的，珍娜，如果不加电池或可选的内存增强器，它也就三磅重。

54
00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:50.610
Yeah.
是啊。

55
00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:54.270
But if you need a battery or optional memory, what is it?
但如果加上电池或可选内存，它得有多重？

56
00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.090
Like 10 pounds?
得有10磅吧？

57
00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:56.610
How heavy is this thing?
这玩意儿到底有多重？

58
00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:00.010
Also, it's got 50L of memory.
而且，它只有50升的内存。

59
00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:00.890
50L.
50升。

60
00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.930
Yeah, you're going to want the booster.
是啊，你肯定会想要那个增强器的。

61
00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.610
We had a fan question from Cameron C.
我们收到一个来自加州卡梅伦·C的粉丝提问。

62
00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:11.590
in California who wanted to know how functional was the Saber Pyramid.
他想知道Saber金字塔到底有多实用。

63
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:19.890
It looks like it might be a non-functional computer screen that you just turn on and off since nobody seems to really use it during the show.
看起来它可能只是个非功能性的电脑屏幕，你只能把它开关一下，因为在节目里似乎没人真正用过它。

64
00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.050
Also, how did they make them?
另外，他们是怎么制作这些东西的？

65
00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:27.610
It seems like a pretty specialized job to cut a screen into a triangle shape.
把屏幕切割成三角形似乎是一项相当专业的工作。

66
00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:30.050
Well, guess who I talked to this morning.
嗯，猜猜我今天早上和谁聊了天。

67
00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.690
Please say Phil Shea.
请说是菲尔·谢伊。

68
00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:32.150
Please.
拜托了。

69
00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:33.610
Phil Shea.
菲尔·谢伊。

70
00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:34.290
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

71
00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.910
Just the loveliest man of all time.
他简直是有史以来最可爱的人。

72
00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.350
He just finished doing a pilot for Justin Spitzer.
他刚为贾斯汀·斯皮策做完一部试播集。

73
00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:43.470
And he mentioned that he ran into you in Bed, Bath & Beyond with the blankets.
他还提到在“家居乐”超市看到你带着毯子。

74
00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:44.090
Yes.
是的。

75
00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.410
He had every shade of gray you could buy.
他买了你能买到的所有灰色调的毯子。

76
00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:47.230
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

77
00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:51.010
Apparently, someone in this pilot has a gray-themed bedroom.
显然，这部试播集里的某个人有个灰色主题的卧室。

78
00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:57.970
Well, Phil told me that the Saber Pyramid was Paul Lieberstein's idea.
嗯，菲尔告诉我，Saber金字塔是保罗·利伯斯坦的主意。

79
00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:07.970
It was going to be a parody of those new tablet computers that were just coming out onto the market at the time of this episode, specifically the Apple iPad.
它原本是想恶搞当时刚上市的新型平板电脑，特别是苹果iPad。

80
00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:11.950
And in the script, all it said was this, quote,
剧本里只写了这么一句，引用如下：

81
00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.990
Dwight holds up the tablet.
德怀特举起平板电脑。

82
00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.530
It is triangle-shaped.
它是三角形的。

83
00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:16.470
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

84
00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.450
Those were the only details.
只有这些细节。

85
00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:24.650
So Phil said that they started by making a bunch of drawings, which they got Paul's approval on.
所以菲尔说，他们先画了一堆草图，并得到了保罗的批准。

86
00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:30.150
And then once they had that, they went to this place called Studio Art and Technology.
一旦确定了方案，他们就去了那家叫“艺术与技术工作室”的地方。

87
00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:36.250
And these guys did, like, a real kind of engineering design of it.
这些人对它进行了真正的工程设计。

88
00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:41.210
And if you can believe it, they printed the case using a 3D printer.
你敢信吗，他们是用3D打印机打印的外壳。

89
00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.190
That's so cool.
太酷了。

90
00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:44.450
Isn't that amazing?
这不是很神奇吗？

91
00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.410
And he said they covered it in plexiglass.
他说他们用有机玻璃覆盖了它。

92
00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:53.150
And they did have one that was functional that actually turned on and lit up.
他们确实有一个能用的，可以开机并点亮。

93
00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:59.370
They even had the capability of different graphics to kind of switch from different screens.
他们甚至有能力切换不同的图形，实现不同屏幕间的转换。

94
00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:04.190
But any of that that you see, that was CGI that was done in poSt.
但你看到的任何画面，都是后期制作的CGI。

95
00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.090
It was not, like, fully functional.
它并不是完全可用的。

96
00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:10.110
It could turn on and show the Saber logo.
它能开机并显示Saber的标志。

97
00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:16.810
And then anything else basically was CGI movement on that screen.
除此之外，屏幕上的其他任何东西基本都是CGI动画。

98
00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:26.790
Phil said they made two of these light-up pyramids because there's a famous saying in the props world, which is, when you have one, you have none.
菲尔说他们做了两个这种能发光的金字塔，因为道具界有句名言：当你只有一个的时候，就等于没有。

99
00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:30.890
Because one means something's going to happen to it, and then you have nothing.
因为只有一个的话，万一出点什么事，你就什么都没有了。

100
00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:31.370
Right.
没错。

101
00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.210
When you have one, you have none.
拥有一个就等于没有。

102
00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:34.510
I kind of like that.
我挺喜欢这句话的。

103
00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:35.170
Right?
对吧？

104
00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:35.810
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

105
00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:41.770
So, anyway, he said later, when we get to some later episodes, you're going to see more of these.
总之，他说以后，等我们聊到后面的剧集时，你们会看到更多这些东西。

106
00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.950
And he gave me the detail about those, too.
他还给了我关于那些东西的细节。

107
00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:44.770
But I'll save it.
但我先卖个关子。

108
00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:45.450
Of course.
当然。

109
00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.630
Why tell you now?
为什么要现在告诉你呢？

110
00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:47.550
Save it.
留着以后说。

111
00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:52.570
Because I have a few tech websites that had their own review of the Saber Pyramid.
因为我有几个科技网站，它们对“军刀金字塔”有自己的评价。

112
00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.490
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

113
00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:55.190
Yes.
是的。

114
00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.290
Not everyone wanted to unleash the power of the pyramid.
并不是每个人都想释放金字塔的力量。

115
00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:05.470
You know, Angela, when I was talking to Phil, he told me a really cool story about James Spader.
安吉拉，你知道吗，我和菲尔聊天时，他跟我讲了一个关于詹姆斯·斯派德的很酷的故事。

116
00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:06.590
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

117
00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:10.950
First of all, he loved working with James, adored him.
首先，他非常喜欢和詹姆斯合作，简直崇拜他。

118
00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:17.870
He said he was, like, such a serious actor and so kind and appreciative with everyone.
他说詹姆斯是一位非常严肃的演员，对每个人都非常友善且懂得感恩。

119
00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:27.570
And he said, you know, for the episode, The List, when Robert California says, I never use a pen, that he only writes in pencil.
他说，在《名单》那一集里，当罗伯特·加州说“我从不用钢笔，只用铅笔书写”时。

120
00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:28.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

121
00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:40.230
He said that James Spader came up to him and said, Phil, could I please get an assortment of different mechanical pencils so that I can choose the exact right one?
他说詹姆斯·斯派德走过来对他说：“菲尔，能帮我找各种不同的自动铅笔吗？这样我才能选出最合适的那一支。”

122
00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:45.290
Because he believed his character had an attachment to, like, a particular mechanical pencil.
因为他认为他的角色对某一种特定的自动铅笔有执念。

123
00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:46.330
But he didn't know.
但他自己也不知道是哪种。

124
00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:48.390
He was like, I'll know it when I see it.
他说：“我看到的时候自然就知道了。”

125
00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:52.830
And so Phil was so excited to go out and buy, like, 12 mechanical pencils.
所以菲尔当时特别兴奋，跑去买了大概12支自动铅笔。

126
00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.810
He made Phil's day.
这让菲尔开心了一整天。

127
00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:56.190
I know.
我知道。

128
00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:57.190
All right.
好了。

129
00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.650
Are you ready for Fast Fact No.
准备好听第二个冷知识了吗？

130
00:06:58.730 --> 00:06:59.050
2?
2？

131
00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:00.390
I am.
准备好了。

132
00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:01.930
Fast Fact No.
第二个冷知识是。

133
00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:05.930
2 is the email that we got from Miles McNutt, Angela.
安吉拉，这是我们收到的一封来自迈尔斯·麦克纳特的邮件。

134
00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:07.850
I loved this email.
我超爱这封邮件。

135
00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:10.430
I have been waiting for us to share it.
我一直等着我们分享它呢。

136
00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.750
Jenna, you have to tell everyone.
珍娜，你一定要告诉大家。

137
00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:13.230
All right.
好的。

138
00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:20.550
Our associate producer Ainsley was going through the office lady's mailbox, and she found this letter from Miles McNutt.
我们的助理制片人安斯利在整理“办公室女士”的邮箱时，发现了这封来自迈尔斯·麦克纳特的信。

139
00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:22.410
And I'm going to read it.
我要读一下。

140
00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:22.910
Ready?
准备好了吗？

141
00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:23.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

142
00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:25.950
He says, greetings.
他说：问候各位。

143
00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:36.030
My friends and followers were kind enough to alert me that my AV Club reviews have made it onto the podcast as the seventh season reaches its conclusion.
我的朋友和粉丝们好心提醒我，随着第七季接近尾声，我的AV Club剧评被搬上了播客。

144
00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:40.810
And I want to thank you for bringing back fond memories of my time covering the show.
我要感谢你们唤起了我报道这部剧时的美好回忆。

145
00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:49.570
I've become a media professor in the intervening period, and Rate My Professors has tagged me as a, quote, tough grader.
在这期间，我已经成为了一名媒体教授，而且在“评价我的教授”网站上，我被贴上了“评分严苛”的标签。

146
00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:53.390
So let the record show that I am nothing if not consistent.
所以请记录在案，我这人一向如此，始终如一。

147
00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:59.130
In the meantime, I look forward to hearing how Jenna felt about my take on the rest of the season,
与此同时，我很期待听到珍娜对我剩余剧集评价的看法，

148
00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:04.370
and highly recommend she stop reading my reviews in season eight for all of our sakes.
