00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:53.910
First of all, we didn't even mention that the day you broke your shoulder, the next
首先，我们还没提到，你摔断肩膀的那天，第二天

310
00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.290
day you had to check out of your condo you were renting.
你就得从租的公寓里搬出来。

311
00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:57.790
They couldn't let you stay.
他们没法让你继续住。

312
00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:58.890
They had someone else coming in.
因为有别人要入住。

313
00:14:59.010 --> 00:15:03.370
And Lee had to pack up all of you guys, and you guys had to find another place to stay.
李不得不帮你们所有人打包行李，你们还得找别的地方住。

314
00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.550
Then you had to find a way out of Aspen.
然后你们得想办法离开阿斯彭。

315
00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:06.790
Then you had to rent a car.
接着还得去租车。

316
00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:09.210
Then the road was closed to a snowstorm.
然后因为暴风雪路封了。

317
00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:14.150
Now you're driving on a curvy, crazy road in a snowstorm three hours out of the way.
现在你们正开在一条弯弯曲曲、疯狂的山路上，在暴风雪中绕了三个小时的路。

318
00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.290
We did not think we were going to make our flight.
我们当时以为赶不上航班了。

319
00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:22.950
We had all these plans to get to Denver, to have dinner, to return our car, to then get
我们原本计划好去丹佛，吃顿晚餐，还车，然后

320
00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:23.890
to this little airport.
赶到那个小机场。

321
00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:26.070
We're like, we're not going to make it.
我们当时想，肯定赶不上了。

322
00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.250
We're in now a blizzard in the mountains.
我们现在正身处山区的暴风雪中。

323
00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.750
I thought we were going to get stuck in the mountains.
我以为我们要被困在山里了。

324
00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:31.930
I started praying.
我开始祈祷。

325
00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:34.190
I was just like, Lord, let him get off that mountain.
我当时就在想，上帝啊，让他平安下山吧。

326
00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:35.690
Just let him get off the mountain.
一定要让他平安下山。

327
00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:36.950
It was so sweet.
太贴心了。

328
00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:41.010
You were just like, I'm in prayer right now for you and for your safe passage.
你当时就说，我正在为你祈祷，祈求你平安通过。

329
00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:43.110
But here's the other thing that Angela did.
但安吉拉还做了另一件事。

330
00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:49.990
Angela and Josh called Josh's mom and Josh's sister and brother-in-law who live in Denver
安吉拉和乔什给住在丹佛的乔什的妈妈、姐姐和姐夫打了电话，

331
00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:50.910
to help us out.
让他们来帮忙。

332
00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:57.070
And they are the reason that we got on this flight because they met us at the entrance
我们能赶上那趟航班全靠他们，因为他们在机场入口处

333
00:15:57.070 --> 00:16:01.810
to the airport with a takeaway dinner of Jersey Mike's.
接应我们，还带了泽西麦克三明治的晚餐。

334
00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:07.790
And they took our car back to the rental place for us because if not for that, we would
他们还帮我们把车开回了租车点，如果不是这样，我们

335
00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:09.370
not have made it on the plane.
根本赶不上飞机。

336
00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:12.790
You had 10 minutes, 10 minutes before our flight.
你们离起飞只剩10分钟，只有10分钟了。

337
00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:15.790
When she texted me, we don't think we're going to make the flight.
当她给我发短信说，我们觉得赶不上航班了。

338
00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:18.530
Maybe we'll get there 10 minutes before if we're lucky.
运气好的话，也许能提前10分钟赶到。

339
00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:21.990
If we can get off this mountain, we'll maybe make it there with 10 minutes to spare.
如果我们能下山，也许能赶在起飞前10分钟到达。

340
00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:25.190
So then I reached out to Josh's family.
所以我联系了乔什的家人。

341
00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:26.330
Josh and I both did.
我和乔什都联系了。

342
00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:28.130
We were like all hands on deck.
我们当时全员出动。

343
00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:30.730
You guys, we've got to get my BFF home.
伙计们，我们得让我最好的朋友回家。

344
00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:31.750
She has a broken shoulder.
她肩膀骨折了。

345
00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:32.810
She needs to get home.
她需要回家。

346
00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.210
And they were amazing.
他们真是太棒了。

347
00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:37.730
Lynn, Nirvon, I mean, Josie, they all stepped up.
琳、尼尔冯，还有乔西，他们都挺身而出。

348
00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:41.750
And Josh's other sister, Jory, in case you got stranded, was like setting up her guest
乔什的另一个姐姐乔里，以防你们被困住，还特意

349
00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:42.470
room for you.
为你们准备了客房。

350
00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:47.430
Angela, it was amazing because when we got there, it was basically like we jumped out
安吉拉，这太神奇了，因为当我们到达时，简直就像是我们直接跳下车一样

351
00:16:47.430 --> 00:16:50.850
of the car and threw them our car keys and grabbed a bag of food.
车里，把车钥匙扔给我们，然后抓起一袋食物。

352
00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:51.890
And we're like, thank you.
我们当时就说，谢谢。

353
00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.290
I mean, we later gave a proper thank you.
我是说，我们后来正式地道了谢。

354
00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:55.390
But it was that crazy.
但当时的情况就是那么疯狂。

355
00:16:55.390 --> 00:17:02.350
Also, big shout out to JSX Airlines and Kevin, who I was on the phone with several times while
另外，还要特别感谢JSX航空和凯文，我在暴风雪的山里时曾多次与他通电话，

356
00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:07.010
in the mountains in a blizzard, who assured me that if I could get there, that they would
他向我保证，只要我能赶到那里，他们就会

357
00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:07.750
let me on the plane.
让我登机。

358
00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:10.790
And I want you to know, they did not know I was Jenna Fisher from the office.
我想让你们知道，他们当时并不知道我是《办公室》里的珍娜·费舍尔。

359
00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:12.930
He was just absolutely wonderful.
他真的非常棒。

360
00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.650
I've never flown this airline before.
我以前从没坐过这家航空公司的飞机。

361
00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:15.610
Incredible.
不可思议。

362
00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.810
Just absolutely amazing.
简直太棒了。

363
00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:19.250
And sure enough, we got there.
果然，我们赶到了那里。

364
00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.330
And we went up to the guy who was letting people on the plane.
我们走到那个负责安排登机的人面前。

365
00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:24.530
And he said, oh, yes, Kevin called.
他说，哦，是的，凯文打过电话了。

366
00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:26.030
He said to expect you.
他说会等你们。

367
00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:29.550
We're like, we're the people with the broken shoulder who were in a blizzard.
我们说，我们就是那个肩膀骨折、困在暴风雪里的人。

368
00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:32.570
So thank you to Josh's family.
所以感谢乔什的家人。

369
00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:34.450
Thank you to Kevin at JSX.
感谢JSX的凯文。

370
00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:38.730
And now I'm going to have a broken shoulder for a while.
现在我的肩膀要骨折一段时间了。

371
00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:40.750
I cannot move my right arm at all.
我的右臂完全动不了。

372
00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:41.590
I cannot move it.
我一点也动不了。

373
00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:44.830
I mean, I went over the other day and I flat ironed your hair for you.
我是说，我前几天过去，还帮你把头发拉直了。

374
00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:45.970
She did.
她确实帮了我。

375
00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:48.550
Yes, grooming has been my biggest challenge.
是的，个人护理成了我最大的挑战。

376
00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:49.690
Grooming and sleeping.
护理和睡觉。

377
00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:50.890
I have to sleep sitting up.
我必须坐着睡觉。

378
00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:51.350
Yeah.
是啊。

379
00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:53.170
Jenna left me the sweetest message.
珍娜给我留了一条最贴心的信息。

380
00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:57.650
She was like, Ange, thank you so much for coming over and flat ironing my hair for me.
她说，安吉，太感谢你过来帮我拉直头发了。

381
00:17:57.710 --> 00:17:59.370
I just needed to feel like a real person.
我只是需要感觉自己像个正常人。

382
00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:04.210
And it just made me think of when we're old ladies and we're going to help each other do things.
这让我想到当我们老了的时候，我们会互相帮助做各种事情。

383
00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:07.090
I did.
我确实这么做了。

384
00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.030
I did.
我确实做了。

385
00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.490
You were there for me with my broken back.
我背部受伤时你就在我身边。

386
00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:12.770
And now you were here for me for my broken shoulder.
现在我肩膀骨折了，你又在我身边。

387
00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:15.310
Lady, I will always be there for you.
亲爱的，我会永远在你身边。

388
00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:18.150
In fact, right now, I think we need to take an ice break.
事实上，现在我觉得我们需要休息一下，冰敷一下。

389
00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.910
Jenna is icing her shoulder as we do the podcaSt.
珍娜在录播客时正在给肩膀冰敷。

390
00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:25.950
And when we come back, we're going to tell you what's really going to incentivize the Dunder Mifflin gang.
等我们回来，我们要告诉你们什么才是真正激励邓德·米夫林员工的东西。

391
00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:27.230
I like it.
我喜欢这个。

392
00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:36.400
We are back.
我们回来了。

393
00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:37.940
And I have a little thing to share with you guys.
我有一件小事要和大家分享。

394
00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:43.140
From the shooting draft, there was a little note on the shooting draft when I went back and looked at it.
在拍摄剧本上，当我回头看的时候，上面有一个小备注。

395
00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:49.380
It said the incentive is episode hashtag 08001.
上面写着《激励》是第08001集。

396
00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.840
And that meant it was the first episode of season eight.
这意味着它是第八季的第一集。

397
00:18:54.000 --> 00:19:01.400
And there was a little note that said, we have decided to air this episode after the list, which was episode number hashtag 08002.
上面有一个小备注写着，我们决定在《名单》之后播出这一集，也就是第08002集。

398
00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:04.160
Those numbers will not change, but this order does.
这些编号不会改变，但播出顺序变了。

399
00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:13.220
Yes, I was watching this episode and when it opens, I thought, why does my belly seem smaller than last week?
是的，我在看这一集的时候，开头我就想，为什么我的肚子看起来比上周小了？

400
00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:17.080
And it's because we shot this episode first, but it aired second.
这是因为我们先拍了这一集，但它是第二集播出的。

401
00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:24.640
In re-watching this episode, Jenna, I forgot what a big storyline Kevin has in this episode.
重看这一集时，珍娜，我忘了凯文在这一集里的戏份竟然这么重。

402
00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:27.480
He has, first of all, he's the whole cold open.
首先，整个开场戏都是他的戏份。

403
00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:35.360
And I'm pretty sure this is one of the most quoted things Brian gets said to him, like of the Kevin line's top five.
而且我敢肯定，这是布莱恩最常被引用的台词之一，大概能排进凯文经典台词的前五名。

404
00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:42.220
It all starts with Jim becoming concerned because Kevin is answering everything in really short sentences.
一切始于吉姆的担忧，因为凯文回答问题时都用极短的句子。

405
00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:46.420
Like, me got it, thank, you know, stuff like that.
比如，我懂了，谢了，你知道的，诸如此类。

406
00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:47.900
And he's like, hmm, what's going on?
吉姆心想，嗯，这是怎么了？

407
00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:53.660
He brings Pam over and the more Kevin talks or actually the less he talks, they're like, okay, you know what?
他把帕姆叫过来，凯文说得越多，或者说他越是不说话，他们就越觉得，好吧，你知道吗？

408
00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:54.840
We need to get you to a hospital.
我们得送你去医院。

409
00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:57.600
And Angela and Oscar are like, no, no, no, he's fine.
安吉拉和奥斯卡却说，不，不，不，他没事。

410
00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:59.080
He's always been like this.
他一直都是这样的。

411
00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:02.220
And Jim and Pam are like, no, no, no, he hasn't always been like this.
吉姆和帕姆说，不，不，不，他以前不是这样的。

412
00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.720
And we're like, yes, he has.
而我们则说，不，他一直都是这样。

413
00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:07.540
Oscar thinks he's making some, you know, statement.
奥斯卡觉得他是在发表什么声明。

414
00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.480
And Angela just thinks this is who he is.
而安吉拉觉得这就是他本来的样子。

415
00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:14.560
And Jim and Pam are like, no, we've got to get to the bottom of this.
吉姆和帕姆坚持说，不行，我们必须查个水落石出。

416
00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:16.560
They bring him into Andy's office.
他们把他带进了安迪的办公室。

417
00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:24.420
And this is where we find out that Kevin has decided he can save a lot of time by speaking with less words.
就在这里我们发现，凯文决定通过少说话来节省大量时间。

418
00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:25.800
That's right.
没错。

419
00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:28.880
And with all of his saved time, he's going to SeaWorld.
而他省下的所有时间，都要用来去海洋世界。

420
00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:30.840
SeaWorld.
海洋世界。

421
00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:33.420
With the fish, not see the world.
是去看鱼的海洋世界，不是去看世界。

422
00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.720
Oh, but he says China.
噢，但他提到了中国。

423
00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:37.020
He does.
确实提到了。

424
00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:43.700
So Jim is really not sure if he means he's going to see the world or go to SeaWorld with all his extra time.
所以吉姆真的不确定他到底是说要去看世界，还是要把省下的时间花在去海洋世界上。

425
00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:47.320
I think this is the line that Brian gets quoted a lot.
我觉得这就是布莱恩最常被引用的那句台词。

426
00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:50.600
Why waste time say lot words when few word do trick?
为什么要浪费时间说那么多话，少说几个词不就行了吗？

427
00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.640
Andy's going to say, here's the deal.
安迪接着说，情况是这样的。

428
00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.840
Kevin, I appreciate what you're trying to do.
凯文，我理解你想做什么。

429
00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:56.480
I really do.
我真的理解。

430
00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.140
But here we have a word code.
但我们这里有语言规范。

431
00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:00.700
Kind of like, you know, how you have a dress code.
就像你们知道的，着装规范那样。

432
00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:08.400
So Andy goes on to say, Kevin, sometime words, you know, need use, but need need for talk talk.
于是安迪继续说，凯文，有时候词语，你知道，需要使用，但没必要说那么多废话。

433
00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:09.540
Yeah.
是啊。

434
00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.220
Kevin's like, fine.
凯文说，好吧。

435
00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:12.520
I'll talk normally.
我会正常说话的。

436
00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:15.360
I have two catches early on.
我早先有两个发现。

437
00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:16.660
I do too.
我也有。

438
00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:19.080
Is yours at one minute, nine seconds?
你的是在一分零九秒吗？

439
00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.220
Mine's at 22 seconds.
我的是在22秒。

440
00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:21.880
What?
什么？

441
00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:23.700
Audi belly button.
奥迪肚脐眼。

442
00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:25.660
You have an Audi?
你有一个奥迪肚脐眼？

443
00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:31.120
You can see my, my belly button from my big old pregnant belly.
你可以从我大大的孕肚上看到我的肚脐眼。

444
00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:38.760
And then at 38 seconds, I want to talk for a moment about your very thin black headband
然后在38秒处，我想聊聊你戴的那条非常细的黑色发带，

445
00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:40.620
that you're wearing, Angela, with your ponytail.
安吉拉，你扎着马尾辫戴着它。

446
00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:41.940
Okay.
好吧。

447
00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:46.640
It's such an interesting look to put this very thin headband on with your ponytail.
扎着马尾辫再戴上这条细发带，看起来真是有趣。

448
00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:47.640
Oh, it's decorative.
噢，那是装饰性的。

449
00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:48.880
It has no job.
它没有任何实际用途。

450
00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:49.520
Right.
没错。

451
00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:50.320
It's just decorative.
这只是装饰用的。

452
00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:51.300
Okay.
好的。

453
00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:52.360
That's all.
就这些了。

454
00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:56.180
I can tell you it's double headache because you have ponytail and headband.
我可以告诉你，因为你扎了马尾又戴了发带，这简直是双重折磨。

455
00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:58.160
This is why I thought it was odd.
这就是为什么我觉得它很奇怪。

456
