612
00:28:16.640 --> 00:28:17.860
It stands for Tuna Dog.
那是金枪鱼狗的意思。

613
00:28:18.820 --> 00:28:20.000
Jim is Tuna Dog.
吉姆是金枪鱼狗。

614
00:28:22.020 --> 00:28:24.060
I kind of wish this had kept going.
我倒希望这段能保留下来。

615
00:28:24.280 --> 00:28:27.880
I wish that every week you would hear someone else's new nickname.
我希望每周你都能听到别人新的绰号。

616
00:28:28.300 --> 00:28:29.460
All dog related.
全都是跟狗有关的。

617
00:28:29.980 --> 00:28:30.420
Apparently.
显然是这样。

618
00:28:31.240 --> 00:28:31.900
Let's see.
我们来看看。

619
00:28:32.040 --> 00:28:34.300
Robert California is going to arrive to the office.
罗伯特·加州要到办公室来了。

620
00:28:34.560 --> 00:28:37.120
He startles Aaron, but he likes Andy's tie.
他吓了艾琳一跳，但他喜欢安迪的领带。

621
00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:38.660
So good job.
所以干得好。

622
00:28:38.920 --> 00:28:40.420
Andy says, hi, dad.
安迪说，嗨，爸爸。

623
00:28:40.540 --> 00:28:41.320
I mean, oh, boy.
我是说，天哪。

624
00:28:43.700 --> 00:28:46.280
Aaron asks Robert if he would like a cold beverage.
艾琳问罗伯特要不要喝点冷饮。

625
00:28:46.440 --> 00:28:47.760
And he says, I'll take a coffee.
他说，我要杯咖啡。

626
00:28:48.120 --> 00:28:55.380
This is going to be troublesome because later she's going to deliver a very, very full cup
这下麻烦了，因为待会儿她会端来满满一杯咖啡，

627
00:28:55.380 --> 00:28:59.600
of coffee that is spilling all over her hands and all over Andy's desk.
咖啡洒得她手上到处都是，安迪的桌子上也全是。

628
00:29:00.200 --> 00:29:03.040
And when Robert takes a sip of it, it is ice cold.
当罗伯特喝了一口时，那咖啡是冰凉的。

629
00:29:03.740 --> 00:29:05.960
And she says, yeah, it's very, very old.
她说，是啊，那咖啡非常非常陈了。

630
00:29:06.200 --> 00:29:06.680
Very old.
非常陈。

631
00:29:06.680 --> 00:29:10.380
This is one of those Aaron moments where I'm like, Aaron, what are you doing?
这是艾琳的那些时刻之一，当时我就想，艾琳，你在干什么？

632
00:29:10.560 --> 00:29:11.840
What are you doing?
你在干什么？

633
00:29:12.180 --> 00:29:14.780
We had a fan question from Naomi W.
我们收到一个来自密歇根州娜奥米·W的粉丝提问，

634
00:29:14.780 --> 00:29:19.600
In Michigan, who said this may sound weird, but was the coffee that Robert California drank
她说这听起来可能很奇怪，但罗伯特·加州喝的那杯咖啡，

635
00:29:19.600 --> 00:29:21.880
and then Andy drank actually cold?
还有后来安迪喝的那杯，真的是冷的吗？

636
00:29:21.880 --> 00:29:23.420
Or was it warm coffee?
还是温热的咖啡？

637
00:29:23.840 --> 00:29:29.740
Naomi, I am going to assume I don't know the answer to this question, but I'm going to assume
娜奥米，我假设我不知道这个问题的答案，但我猜，

638
00:29:29.740 --> 00:29:32.240
that it was a room temp coffee.
那应该是常温咖啡。

639
00:29:32.520 --> 00:29:38.380
They would be very nervous about giving us like a hot beverage in a scene for so many
剧组会因为很多原因，对在拍摄现场给我们提供热饮感到非常紧张，

640
00:29:38.380 --> 00:29:41.760
reasons, but they would not have served a cold beverage.
但他们也不会提供冷饮。

641
00:29:41.980 --> 00:29:45.720
They would not have served like old ice cold coffee.
他们不会提供那种陈年的冰咖啡。

642
00:29:45.720 --> 00:29:48.980
So I'm guessing, but that would be my guess.
所以我只是猜测，但这会是我的猜测。

643
00:29:49.640 --> 00:29:56.200
Well, somewhere in this cold old coffee drinking, Robert's going to realize that Andy likes Aaron
好吧，就在这喝着陈年冷咖啡的过程中，罗伯特会意识到安迪喜欢艾琳，

644
00:29:56.200 --> 00:29:57.820
and Aaron likes Andy.
而艾琳也喜欢安迪。

645
00:29:58.020 --> 00:29:59.620
And Andy's like, yeah, you know what?
安迪说，是啊，你知道吗？

646
00:29:59.740 --> 00:30:02.560
We just the timing has never quite been right.
我们只是时机一直不太对。

647
00:30:02.560 --> 00:30:03.540
I mean, I liked her.
我是说，我喜欢她。

648
00:30:03.740 --> 00:30:05.280
And Robert's like, I've lost intereSt.
罗伯特说，我没兴趣了。

649
00:30:05.900 --> 00:30:06.040
Yeah.
是啊。

650
00:30:06.740 --> 00:30:07.340
That's it.
就是这样。

651
00:30:07.460 --> 00:30:07.880
He's done.
他讲完了。

652
00:30:08.600 --> 00:30:09.780
Well, Robert is all business.
罗伯特这个人公事公办。

653
00:30:10.140 --> 00:30:15.580
He goes out into the bullpen and he is going to give what is a kind of inspirational speech
他走到办公区，准备发表一番鼓舞人心的演讲，

654
00:30:15.580 --> 00:30:21.520
about why do people choose a small paper company over a big superstore?
关于为什么人们会选择小型造纸公司而不是大型超市？

655
00:30:21.840 --> 00:30:23.880
And it's because of the service.
答案就是服务。

656
00:30:23.960 --> 00:30:25.520
It's the personal service.
是个性化服务。

657
00:30:25.520 --> 00:30:28.540
And he says, now I'm going to give you a challenge.
他说，现在我要给你们一个挑战。

658
00:30:28.540 --> 00:30:30.200
I want you to double your sales.
我要你们把销售额翻倍。

659
00:30:30.200 --> 00:30:33.280
This quarter, you have one quarter, double your sales.
这个季度，你们有一个季度的时间，把销售额翻倍。

660
00:30:33.800 --> 00:30:37.220
Everybody is completely captivated by him.
每个人都被他深深吸引住了。

661
00:30:37.800 --> 00:30:39.360
We look like we're in awe.
我们看起来就像被震慑住了一样。

662
00:30:39.560 --> 00:30:42.020
We look like we would have just followed him right off a cliff.
看起来如果他带头跳崖，我们也会跟着跳下去。

663
00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:48.680
So this scene was the very first scene that we shot with James Spader for season eight.
所以这一幕是我们第八季和詹姆斯·斯派德拍摄的第一场戏。

664
00:30:48.680 --> 00:30:51.100
And I will never forget it.
我永远不会忘记。

665
00:30:51.360 --> 00:30:53.600
We were captivated by him.
我们被他迷住了。

666
00:30:53.620 --> 00:30:55.520
We were in awe of him.
我们对他肃然起敬。

667
00:30:55.840 --> 00:30:59.940
All of our reactions of standing there and just being mesmerized by him
我们所有人站在那儿被他深深吸引的反应，

668
00:30:59.940 --> 00:31:02.040
were because we actually were in real life.
是因为在现实生活中我们确实如此。

669
00:31:02.860 --> 00:31:06.700
I mean, he was completely captivating as a human being.
我是说，作为一个人，他非常有魅力。

670
00:31:07.320 --> 00:31:07.440
Yeah.
没错。

671
00:31:07.620 --> 00:31:11.360
Whenever he had a big speech to the bullpen and we all had to be there, all I could think
每当他要在办公区发表长篇大论，而我们都必须在场时，我满脑子想的

672
00:31:11.360 --> 00:31:14.740
of was like, whatever you do, don't break or laugh.
都是：不管怎样，千万别笑场。

673
00:31:14.940 --> 00:31:18.600
Not that I would because I was like, you know, slightly in awe slash terrified.
倒不是说我会笑，因为我当时既敬畏又有点害怕。

674
00:31:19.100 --> 00:31:24.220
But then also, like, I'd be like, oh, please don't let me have a weird gurgle or weird belly
但同时我也会想，噢，千万别让我发出什么奇怪的咕噜声或者肚子

675
00:31:24.220 --> 00:31:24.580
noise.
叫声。

676
00:31:24.580 --> 00:31:25.500
I don't know.
我不知道。

677
00:31:25.660 --> 00:31:26.880
I was wearing that fake belly.
我当时戴着那个假肚子。

678
00:31:27.120 --> 00:31:28.340
It was pushing up on me.
它一直顶着我。

679
00:31:28.680 --> 00:31:30.640
I was gurgly during this time.
那段时间我肚子总是在咕噜响。

680
00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:34.860
I just know that like when I'm acting with someone, I'm pretty good at staying in the
我只知道，当我和别人演对手戏时，我挺擅长沉浸在

681
00:31:34.860 --> 00:31:35.120
moment.
当下。

682
00:31:35.280 --> 00:31:39.820
I'm pretty good at staying in my character and seeing them as their character and kind of
我挺擅长保持角色状态，把对方看作剧中人物，并让自己

683
00:31:39.820 --> 00:31:40.820
staying in the story.
留在故事里。

684
00:31:41.280 --> 00:31:45.620
But every once in a while, there are actors that I've worked with that I can't help but
但偶尔也会遇到一些合作过的演员，让我忍不住

685
00:31:45.620 --> 00:31:48.840
sort of like leave my body and watch us from the outside.
灵魂出窍，从旁观者的角度看我们演戏。

686
00:31:49.080 --> 00:31:49.380
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

687
00:31:49.560 --> 00:31:51.280
This would happen to me a lot with John C.
我和约翰·C·赖利

688
00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:51.700
Reilly.
合作时经常这样。

689
00:31:51.920 --> 00:31:53.780
Just it would be my turn to talk.
轮到我说话了，

690
00:31:53.960 --> 00:31:57.740
And I would just be like, oh, my God, I'm so sorry I was watching us.
我却会想，天哪，抱歉，我刚才在看我们演戏。

691
00:31:58.120 --> 00:32:03.500
I forgot that this wasn't like a solo performance for me, that I'm actually in this scene.
我忘了这不是我一个人的独角戏，我其实也在戏里。

692
00:32:03.820 --> 00:32:06.460
And that would happen to me a lot with James Spader.
和詹姆斯·斯派德合作时也经常发生这种情况。

693
00:32:06.460 --> 00:32:10.300
A lot of the time, I would just like get caught up in his performance.
很多时候，我都会沉浸在他的表演里。

694
00:32:11.560 --> 00:32:12.580
Yeah, me too.
没错，我也是。

695
00:32:12.840 --> 00:32:17.540
That happened a lot, too, for me with Will Ferrell, because I would just watch him be
我和威尔·法瑞尔合作时也经常这样，因为我总是看着他，觉得他

696
00:32:17.540 --> 00:32:18.020
so funny.
太搞笑了。

697
00:32:18.100 --> 00:32:20.340
And I'd be like, oh, God, I'm supposed to say something here.
然后我会想，天哪，我该接话了。

698
00:32:21.340 --> 00:32:23.900
Robert is going to leave after he gives this mandate.
罗伯特下达完指令后就会离开。

699
00:32:24.260 --> 00:32:29.240
And Andy is going to very awkwardly sit on Jim's desk.
而安迪会非常尴尬地坐在吉姆的桌子上。

700
00:32:29.880 --> 00:32:32.940
When I saw this, I had to know, was that scripted?
看到这一幕时，我必须得问，那是剧本里写的吗？

701
00:32:33.280 --> 00:32:34.560
Was it improv?
那是即兴发挥吗？

702
00:32:34.560 --> 00:32:35.840
Pav, I couldn't remember.
帕夫，我记不清了。

703
00:32:36.160 --> 00:32:37.320
I went to the script.
我查了剧本。

704
00:32:38.080 --> 00:32:39.160
It scripted.
那是剧本写的。

705
00:32:39.360 --> 00:32:44.960
I did, too, because I thought, I mean, is Ed just deciding to saddle up on Jim's desk
我也查了，因为我在想，我是说，是艾德决定要骑到吉姆的桌子上吗？

706
00:32:44.960 --> 00:32:46.920
like awkwardly and shove things aside?
动作还那么笨拙，把东西都推开？

707
00:32:46.920 --> 00:32:47.940
Was this written?
这是写好的吗？

708
00:32:48.140 --> 00:32:48.760
Was that Ed?
那是艾德自己的主意吗？

709
00:32:48.920 --> 00:32:50.040
And Jenna, I did the same thing.
珍娜，我也做了同样的事。

710
00:32:50.240 --> 00:32:56.160
The script says Andy leans up against Jim's desk and then very awkwardly begins to sit on
剧本上写着安迪靠在吉姆的桌子上，然后非常笨拙地开始坐在

711
00:32:56.160 --> 00:33:00.840
Jim's desk, knocking over a few things and shoving some stuff onto Dwight's desk.
吉姆的桌子上，撞倒了一些东西，还把一些杂物推到了德怀特的桌子上。

712
00:33:01.280 --> 00:33:02.860
Phyllis rolls her eyes.
菲利斯翻了个白眼。

713
00:33:02.860 --> 00:33:03.660
Yeah.
没错。

714
00:33:04.040 --> 00:33:11.700
You know, also during this, I noticed that Dwight is holding the bamboo plant in his lap.
你知道，在这期间我还注意到，德怀特把那盆竹子抱在怀里。

715
00:33:12.180 --> 00:33:15.480
And again, I was like, what's happening with that?
我当时又在想，那是在干什么？

716
00:33:15.640 --> 00:33:17.200
And I was not the only one.
而且不止我一个人这么想。

717
00:33:17.380 --> 00:33:24.120
We got a fan question from Chloe F in Maryland who said, what's up with Dwight's bamboo when
我们收到了一位来自马里兰州的粉丝克洛伊·F的提问，她说，当

718
00:33:24.120 --> 00:33:26.040
Andy is sitting on Jim's desk?
安迪坐在吉姆桌子上时，德怀特的竹子是怎么回事？

719
00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:28.700
Why does he hold it in front of his face?
他为什么要把它挡在脸前面？

720
00:33:28.700 --> 00:33:29.980
I can't stop laughing.
我笑得停不下来。

721
00:33:30.660 --> 00:33:31.120
Okay.
好吧。

722
00:33:31.260 --> 00:33:36.100
So at first I thought he picked up the plant to protect it because Andy's knocking everything
起初我以为他拿起那盆植物是为了保护它，因为安迪把所有东西都

723
00:33:36.100 --> 00:33:36.600
off.
撞掉了。

724
00:33:36.860 --> 00:33:37.260
Right.
对。

725
00:33:37.520 --> 00:33:38.400
It's not the case.
事实并非如此。

726
00:33:38.780 --> 00:33:39.920
Not the case.
并非如此。

727
00:33:40.140 --> 00:33:43.100
Went to the script and there was a note about it.
我查了剧本，上面确实有一条关于这个的备注。

728
00:33:43.360 --> 00:33:43.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

729
00:33:44.320 --> 00:33:45.340
Did you see it as well?
你也看到了吗？

730
00:33:45.480 --> 00:33:45.880
I did.
我看到了。

731
00:33:46.080 --> 00:33:46.600
You read it.
你读到了。

732
00:33:47.040 --> 00:33:47.540
All right.
好吧。

733
00:33:47.800 --> 00:33:52.620
It just said, Andy watches Dwight who is sniffing a flowerless plant.
上面只写着，安迪看着正在闻一盆没开花的植物的德怀特。

734
00:33:52.620 --> 00:33:59.880
But lady, I have to say, in rereading the shooting draft, Dwight has some real odd behavior in
但是女士，我不得不说，在重读拍摄剧本时，德怀特在

735
00:33:59.880 --> 00:34:00.480
this episode.
这一集里有一些非常奇怪的行为。

736
00:34:00.660 --> 00:34:04.080
And I know part of it is because he's just decided to check out.
我知道部分原因是由于他决定要置身事外。

737
00:34:04.520 --> 00:34:07.980
But there are some really random scenes with Dwight.
但德怀特确实有一些非常随意的场景。

738
00:34:08.620 --> 00:34:13.100
There's one later that I'm going to play for you because I was like, what is happening
后面还有一个场景，我要放给你听，因为当时我在想，德怀特

739
00:34:13.100 --> 00:34:13.800
with Dwight?
到底在干什么？

740
00:34:13.940 --> 00:34:15.020
It's in deleted scenes.
那是在删减片段里。

741
00:34:15.880 --> 00:34:18.060
About this time, Justine is going to arrive.
大约在这个时候，贾斯汀要到了。

742
00:34:18.520 --> 00:34:19.860
Kevin doesn't know what to do.
凯文不知道该怎么办。

743
00:34:20.040 --> 00:34:21.480
I guess he's alone at front reception.
我猜他当时独自在前台。

744
00:34:21.480 --> 00:34:22.380
He has a meltdown.
他崩溃了。

745
00:34:22.540 --> 00:34:24.820
He just starts yelling, Daryl, girl.
他开始大喊，达里尔，女孩。

746
00:34:25.760 --> 00:34:26.180
Yes.
是的。

747
00:34:26.660 --> 00:34:29.080
Justine was played by Erica Vatina Phillips.
贾斯汀由埃里卡·瓦蒂娜·菲利普斯饰演。

748
00:34:29.160 --> 00:34:34.240
You probably remember her from Superbad, the 40-year-old virgin, Veep.
你可能在《太坏了》、《四十岁的老处男》和《副总统》中记得她。

749
00:34:34.820 --> 00:34:37.440
Her scene in the 40-year-old virgin, I will never forget it.
她在《四十岁的老处男》里的那场戏，我永远不会忘记。

750
00:34:37.520 --> 00:34:38.740
It is so funny.
太搞笑了。

751
00:34:39.140 --> 00:34:40.580
It is so, so funny.
真的，真的太搞笑了。

752
00:34:40.760 --> 00:34:41.280
Google it.
去谷歌搜一下吧。

753
00:34:41.600 --> 00:34:44.840
Like, just give yourself a laugh break.
就当是给自己放个笑话假。

754
00:34:45.100 --> 00:34:46.260
You won't be sorry.
你绝对不会后悔的。

755
00:34:46.840 --> 00:34:48.020
That's all I'm going to say.
我只能说这么多了。

756
00:34:48.140 --> 00:34:48.940
I don't want to ruin it.
我不想剧透。

757
00:34:49.240 --> 00:34:49.480
Okay.
好吧。

758
00:34:49.960 --> 00:34:52.340
Well, Daryl is so giddy that she's there.
达里尔看到她在那里，简直乐坏了。

759
00:34:52.520 --> 00:34:53.960
He, like, winks to the camera.
他甚至还对着镜头眨眼。

760
00:34:53.960 --> 00:34:55.240
They go in his office.
他们进了他的办公室。

761
00:34:55.640 --> 00:34:56.100
Yeah.
没错。

762
00:34:56.300 --> 00:34:56.620
Shuts the door.
关上了门。

763
00:34:56.860 --> 00:34:58.520
He's very excited.
他非常兴奋。

764
00:34:58.780 --> 00:35:00.440
But then we never see her again.
但之后我们就再也没见过她了。

765
00:35:00.600 --> 00:35:00.920
Yeah.
是啊。

766
00:35:01.100 --> 00:35:01.800
That's what I was going to say.
我正想说这个呢。

767
00:35:01.800 --> 00:35:02.880
Or mention her at all.
甚至连提都没提过她。

768
00:35:03.200 --> 00:35:04.360
Where is she?
她去哪儿了？

769
00:35:04.400 --> 00:35:06.140
Is she just in his office for the whole episode?
她难道整集都待在他办公室里吗？

770
00:35:06.140 --> 00:35:06.920
What's happening?
到底发生了什么？

771
00:35:07.280 --> 00:35:08.960
We weren't the only ones, Angela.
安吉拉，不只是我们这么想。

772
00:35:09.260 --> 00:35:14.000
Fan question from Soyeon Jae, who is from South Korea but currently living in Germany,
来自韩国目前住在德国的Soyeon Jae提问，

773
00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:18.540
who wrote in to say the storyline with Justine ended so abruptly in this episode.
她写信来说贾斯汀的故事线在这一集结束得太突然了。

774
00:35:19.100 --> 00:35:22.300
Did she appear just as buildup for the next episode?
她出现只是为了给下一集做铺垫吗？

775
00:35:22.560 --> 00:35:23.300
What happened?
到底发生了什么？

776
00:35:24.180 --> 00:35:26.080
Well, we both went to the shooting draft.
嗯，我们俩都去查了拍摄剧本。

777
00:35:26.260 --> 00:35:27.300
There is a whole scene.
其实有一整场戏。

778
00:35:27.520 --> 00:35:29.400
It's actually in deleted scenes.
就在删减片段里。

779
00:35:29.400 --> 00:35:30.440
And I thought we could hear it.
我想我们可以听听看。

780
00:35:30.580 --> 00:35:31.620
It explains everything.
它解释了一切。

781
00:35:32.020 --> 00:35:32.860
Let's hear it.
我们来听听吧。

782
00:35:33.360 --> 00:35:35.180
Jada called me during recess.
贾达课间休息时给我打了电话。

783
00:35:35.680 --> 00:35:37.440
She asked me when you're moving back in.
她问我你什么时候搬回来。

784
00:35:38.040 --> 00:35:39.460
What did you say to our daughter?
你跟我们女儿说什么了？

785
00:35:40.140 --> 00:35:41.500
That we're getting back together?
说我们要复合了？

786
00:35:42.180 --> 00:35:43.900
I just didn't calm down.
我当时就是没冷静下来。

787
00:35:44.100 --> 00:35:44.900
One night together.
共度了一晚。

788
00:35:45.140 --> 00:35:46.220
And you think it's on.
你就觉得我们要成了。

789
00:35:47.120 --> 00:35:47.900
You're an idiot.
你真是个白痴。

790
00:35:48.300 --> 00:35:49.880
I told you it was a one-time thing.
我告诉过你那只是一次性的。

791
00:35:49.980 --> 00:35:50.940
Last night was good, right?
昨晚感觉不错，对吧？

792
00:35:51.240 --> 00:35:52.880
I said, touch and go, Daryl.
我说过，达里尔，那是“触碰即走”。

793
00:35:53.040 --> 00:35:55.000
You get a little touch and then you go.
你稍微碰一下，然后就得走。

794
00:35:55.900 --> 00:35:57.160
Stay the hell away from me.
离我远点。

795
00:35:59.230 --> 00:36:00.250
Touch and go.
触碰即走。

796
00:36:00.470 --> 00:36:01.210
Touch and go.
触碰即走。

797
00:36:01.370 --> 00:36:03.670
You get a little touch, then you gots to go.
稍微碰一下，然后你就得走人。

798
00:36:04.390 --> 00:36:06.070
I love this expression.
我喜欢这个表达。

799
00:36:06.070 --> 00:36:06.670
I know.
我知道。

800
00:36:06.950 --> 00:36:09.170
I'm looking for a touch and go relationship.
我正在寻找一段“触碰即走”的关系。

801
00:36:09.550 --> 00:36:11.650
I'm hot to trot and I need some touch and go.
我迫不及待想大干一场了。

802
00:36:12.150 --> 00:36:13.690
Oh, there it is.
哦，原来在这儿。

803
00:36:15.790 --> 00:36:20.570
So, yeah, in the shooting draft, it said the minute the door shuts, you start to hear her
所以，剧本初稿里写的是，门一关上，你就能听到她

804
00:36:20.570 --> 00:36:24.470
scream at him because he's told their daughter they're getting back together.
对他大吼大叫，因为他告诉女儿他们要复合了。

805
00:36:24.690 --> 00:36:25.230
She's furious.
她气疯了。

806
00:36:25.550 --> 00:36:28.550
And the whole entire bullpen hears their argument.
整个办公区的人都听到了他们的争吵。

807
00:36:28.810 --> 00:36:31.870
And so there's a lot of reaction shots of people like, awkward.
所以有很多大家尴尬反应的镜头。

808
00:36:32.510 --> 00:36:34.190
And then she storms out.
然后她冲了出去。

809
00:36:34.330 --> 00:36:35.810
So we know that she's left.
所以我们知道她离开了。

810
00:36:35.970 --> 00:36:39.350
Instead of me wondering this whole episode, where has this woman gone?
这样我就不用整集都在想，这个女人去哪儿了？

811
00:36:39.350 --> 00:36:40.710
Is she still in Daryl's office?
她还在达里尔的办公室吗？

812
00:36:41.070 --> 00:36:41.210
Yeah.
是的。

813
00:36:41.890 --> 00:36:45.050
Up next is another Dwight moment that's super random.
接下来是另一个德怀特的时刻，非常随机。

814
00:36:45.310 --> 00:36:47.150
He's in the kitchen making brownies.
他在厨房里做布朗尼。

815
00:36:47.410 --> 00:36:48.690
And Andy's going to walk in.
安迪会走进来。

816
00:36:48.810 --> 00:36:51.870
And it's clear that he's just trying to figure out how do we double sales.
很明显他只是在想怎么把销售额翻倍。

817
00:36:52.310 --> 00:36:52.710
Yeah.
没错。

818
00:36:52.810 --> 00:36:55.190
He wants Dwight to do the work for him, basically.
他基本上是想让德怀特替他干活。

819
00:36:55.950 --> 00:36:57.310
I have a lot of questions.
我有很多问题。

820
00:36:57.870 --> 00:36:58.710
About this scene?
关于这场戏吗？

821
00:36:59.270 --> 00:36:59.710
Yes.
是的。

822
00:37:00.090 --> 00:37:01.070
Can I just say one thing?
我能先说一件事吗？

823
00:37:01.150 --> 00:37:03.130
What if you're like, no, Angela, not about this scene?
要是你说“不，安吉拉，不是关于这场戏”怎么办？

824
00:37:05.270 --> 00:37:06.330
Just about life.
只是关于人生。

825
00:37:06.530 --> 00:37:06.890
I know.
我知道。

826
00:37:06.950 --> 00:37:07.850
I have questions about life.
我对人生有很多疑问。

827
00:37:07.890 --> 00:37:07.990
I know.
我知道。

828
00:37:09.670 --> 00:37:10.570
Here's my question.
我的问题是这个。

829
00:37:11.670 --> 00:37:13.270
Where is he baking these brownies?
他是在哪儿烤这些布朗尼的？

830
00:37:13.450 --> 00:37:14.510
We do not have an oven.
我们根本没有烤箱。

831
00:37:14.830 --> 00:37:16.770
Is this a microwave brownie recipe?
这是微波炉布朗尼食谱吗？

832
00:37:17.390 --> 00:37:18.030
It's got to be.
肯定是。

833
00:37:18.030 --> 00:37:21.390
I also have known Greg Daniels to make brownies in a microwave.
我也知道格雷格·丹尼尔斯曾用微波炉做过布朗尼。

834
00:37:21.830 --> 00:37:22.270
Just saying.
我只是提一下。

835
00:37:22.690 --> 00:37:25.690
In like a mug or in a pan?
是用马克杯还是烤盘？

836
00:37:25.870 --> 00:37:26.830
I don't know how he did it.
我不知道他是怎么做的。

837
00:37:26.910 --> 00:37:29.330
I just remember one time him trying to figure that out.
我只记得有一次他在研究这个。

838
00:37:29.710 --> 00:37:30.230
All right.
好吧。

839
00:37:30.430 --> 00:37:34.830
Well, I got very curious about brownies in general.
总之，我对布朗尼产生了浓厚的兴趣。

840
00:37:35.470 --> 00:37:39.650
Because, you know, at the end of the scene, Dwight is going to dump a bunch of nuts into
因为，你知道，在这一幕的结尾，德怀特会往

841
00:37:39.650 --> 00:37:40.370
the brownies.
布朗尼里倒一大堆坚果。

842
00:37:40.670 --> 00:37:41.030
Walnuts.
核桃。

843
00:37:41.110 --> 00:37:42.850
And Kevin has a big reaction.
凯文的反应很大。

844
00:37:43.270 --> 00:37:43.550
Yeah.
没错。

845
00:37:43.790 --> 00:37:44.630
Big old walnuts.
大块的核桃。

846
00:37:44.630 --> 00:37:46.830
Kevin's like, no, I'm with you, Kevin.
凯文当时的样子，不，凯文，我支持你。

847
00:37:47.090 --> 00:37:48.990
I don't want a big walnut in my brownie.
我可不想在布朗尼里吃到大核桃。

848
00:37:49.470 --> 00:37:49.730
Okay.
好吧。

849
00:37:50.210 --> 00:37:50.730
Same.
我也是。

850
00:37:51.190 --> 00:37:53.570
I don't like nuts and brownies.
我不喜欢布朗尼里有坚果。

851
00:37:54.230 --> 00:37:58.570
And I wanted to know, how did the nut get in the brownie?
我想知道，布朗尼里的坚果是怎么来的？

852
00:37:59.070 --> 00:38:01.110
Was it part of the original recipe?
它是原始配方的一部分吗？

853
00:38:01.270 --> 00:38:04.150
Or was this an addition that somebody made?
还是后来有人加进去的？

854
00:38:04.550 --> 00:38:08.190
So I deep dived the origin story of the brownie.
所以我深入挖掘了布朗尼的起源故事。

855
00:38:08.810 --> 00:38:11.090
Please, please share with me what you found.
求求你，快跟我分享一下你发现了什么。

856
00:38:11.270 --> 00:38:13.970
This is nowhere where I thought we would go today.
这完全出乎我的意料，没想到我们今天会聊到这个。

857
00:38:13.970 --> 00:38:16.690
And I'm getting my cup of tea and settling in.
我这就去拿杯茶，准备好好听听。

858
00:38:16.990 --> 00:38:18.630
Well, here's what I'll tell you.
好吧，我来告诉你。

859
00:38:18.870 --> 00:38:22.410
The brownie is believed to have been invented in the United States.
人们认为布朗尼是在美国发明的。

860
00:38:22.770 --> 00:38:23.930
In Boston.
在波士顿。

861
00:38:25.050 --> 00:38:30.570
The first brownie recipe is believed to belong to Fanny Farmer.
第一份布朗尼配方被认为是出自范妮·法默之手。

862
00:38:30.890 --> 00:38:36.510
Let me go on a tangent about this badass boss lady named Fanny Farmer.
让我跑个题，讲讲这位名叫范妮·法默的厉害女强人。

863
00:38:36.690 --> 00:38:40.690
I'm not sure I've been so excited about someone since we learned about Clementine Paddleford.
自从了解了克莱门汀·帕德尔福德之后，我还没对谁这么兴奋过。

864
00:38:40.690 --> 00:38:42.450
I have a painting of her.
我有一张她的画像。

865
00:38:42.630 --> 00:38:44.430
Clementine, I stare at her every day.
克莱门汀，我每天都盯着她看。

866
00:38:44.770 --> 00:38:54.650
Well, I might get a painting of Fanny Farmer for my office because Fanny grew up in like the 1800s, the late 1800s.
嗯，我可能得给办公室也弄一张范妮·法默的画像，因为范妮是在19世纪，也就是19世纪末长大的。

867
00:38:54.650 --> 00:39:01.030
But she came from a family that really valued education for both the boys and the girls in the family.
她出身于一个非常重视子女教育的家庭，无论男孩还是女孩。

868
00:39:01.430 --> 00:39:02.610
So this was rather progressive.
这在当时相当进步。

869
00:39:03.310 --> 00:39:09.790
However, when she was 16 years old, she suffered a stroke and it left her unable to walk for several years.
然而，她在16岁时中风了，导致几年内无法行走。

870
00:39:09.990 --> 00:39:13.630
And she was not able to go to college as her family had hoped.
她没能像家人期望的那样去上大学。

871
00:39:13.630 --> 00:39:18.570
So she lived with her family and she started cooking and baking.
于是她和家人住在一起，开始钻研烹饪和烘焙。

872
00:39:19.050 --> 00:39:27.390
Her parents ran a boarding house and she actually became very, very well known for her recipes at this boarding house.
她的父母经营着一家寄宿公寓，而她凭借在那里的出色厨艺变得非常、非常有名。

873
00:39:27.630 --> 00:39:38.690
So much so that when she turned 30 years old and she was able to move again, she enrolled at the Boston Cooking School.
名气大到什么程度呢？当她30岁能重新走动时，她进入了波士顿烹饪学校学习。

874
00:39:38.690 --> 00:39:41.030
And she was one of their best students.
她是学校里最优秀的学生之一。

875
00:39:41.310 --> 00:39:43.490
And this cooking school was also very progressive.
这所烹饪学校也非常进步。

876
00:39:43.710 --> 00:39:49.990
They really believed in the idea of like food and nutrition and how that contributed to your overall health.
他们非常推崇食物与营养的理念，以及它们如何影响整体健康。

877
00:39:50.470 --> 00:39:53.570
And she was so good that she ended up becoming a teacher.
她表现得太出色了，最后留校任教。

878
00:39:53.650 --> 00:39:56.470
And then she became the principal of the school.
后来她还成了学校的校长。

879
00:39:56.850 --> 00:40:03.170
And when she was the principal of the school, she released a cookbook called the Boston Cooking School Cookbook.
在担任校长期间，她出版了一本名为《波士顿烹饪学校食谱》的书。

880
00:40:03.170 --> 00:40:10.030
The book's publisher was a company called Little Brown and Company, and they didn't think that the cookbook would do any sales.
这本书的出版商是一家叫“小布朗公司”的企业，他们当时觉得这本食谱卖不出去。

881
00:40:10.310 --> 00:40:16.050
So they only published 3000 copies of the cookbook and they charged Fanny for them.
所以他们只印了3000本，而且还让范妮自己掏钱买下这些书。

882
00:40:16.170 --> 00:40:18.790
They made her pay for the cookbooks.
他们让她自费出版。

883
00:40:19.050 --> 00:40:22.330
It was basically like a self-publishing thing.
这基本上就是一种自费出版的形式。

884
00:40:22.610 --> 00:40:22.750
Yeah.
没错。

885
00:40:23.430 --> 00:40:24.270
Listen to this.
听听这个。

886
00:40:24.470 --> 00:40:30.010
The book was so popular that it is still in print over 100 years later.
这本书太受欢迎了，一百多年后的今天仍在印刷。

887
00:40:30.010 --> 00:40:35.630
It has been through multiple reprints and now it's called the Fanny Farmer Cookbook.
它经历了多次再版，现在被称为《范妮·法默食谱》。

888
00:40:35.870 --> 00:40:36.830
You know what I say?
你知道我想说什么吗？

889
00:40:36.950 --> 00:40:37.590
Good for you.
干得漂亮。

890
00:40:37.710 --> 00:40:39.230
Good for you, Fanny Farmer.
干得漂亮，范妮·法默。

891
00:40:39.490 --> 00:40:40.170
Good for you.
干得漂亮。

892
00:40:40.570 --> 00:40:42.170
You made a wicked cookbook.
你写了一本超棒的食谱。

893
00:40:42.410 --> 00:40:43.190
Good for you.
干得漂亮。

894
00:40:43.570 --> 00:40:44.390
That's right.
说得对。

895
00:40:44.930 --> 00:40:46.570
I am so proud of her.
我真为她感到骄傲。

896
00:40:47.050 --> 00:40:48.870
Sorry for my Boston accent.
抱歉，我刚才用了波士顿口音。

897
00:40:49.050 --> 00:40:50.010
You guys, I couldn't resiSt.
伙计们，我实在忍不住。

898
00:40:50.270 --> 00:40:50.750
I couldn't.
我忍不住。

899
00:40:50.970 --> 00:40:52.590
So back to the brownie.
好了，回到布朗尼的话题。

900
00:40:53.030 --> 00:40:56.150
It is believed that Fanny invented the brownie.
人们认为正是范妮发明了布朗尼。

901
00:40:56.150 --> 00:41:05.450
In 1905, she adapted a chocolate cookie recipe into a bar cookie, which is believed to be the first brownie.
1905年，她将一款巧克力曲奇的配方改良成了块状曲奇，这被认为是第一款布朗尼。

902
00:41:05.710 --> 00:41:13.890
The second brownie recipe appeared in a cookbook in 1907, and it was made by Maria Willett Howard.
第二款布朗尼配方出现在1907年的一本食谱中，是由玛丽亚·威利特·霍华德制作的。

903
00:41:14.190 --> 00:41:21.670
Maria was a protege of Fanny Farmer, and she adapted the recipe by adding an extra egg and an extra square of chocolate.
玛丽亚是范妮·法默的学生，她通过多加一个鸡蛋和一块巧克力对配方进行了改良。

904
00:41:21.670 --> 00:41:27.150
And it is really the second recipe that is most like the brownie we eat today.
事实上，正是这第二款配方最接近我们今天吃的布朗尼。

905
00:41:27.410 --> 00:41:39.270
And the reason that I have told you all of this information about Fanny and about Maria is because neither of these two original brownie recipes contained any nuts,
我之所以告诉你们所有关于范妮和玛丽亚的信息，是因为这两款最初的布朗尼配方里都没有坚果，

906
00:41:39.270 --> 00:41:42.010
which means that you and I are right, Angela.
这意味着安吉拉，你和我是对的。

907
00:41:42.230 --> 00:41:43.890
Nuts do not belong in brownies.
布朗尼里不该放坚果。

908
00:41:44.130 --> 00:41:46.270
Thank you, Fanny and Maria.
谢谢你们，范妮和玛丽亚。

909
00:41:46.770 --> 00:41:47.430
Thank you.
谢谢。

910
00:41:47.890 --> 00:41:48.770
Yes, thank you.
没错，谢谢。

911
00:41:49.390 --> 00:41:51.190
Well, guess what we have next?
好了，猜猜接下来是什么？

912
00:41:51.190 --> 00:41:54.270
Next, we have a little Big Pregs, Little Pregs storyline.
接下来是一段关于“大孕妇”和“小孕妇”的剧情。

913
00:41:55.170 --> 00:42:03.250
Angela is going to hand Pam the current issue of Parent Magazine and wants to know if she read the article about the importance of regular walks.
安吉拉把最新一期的《父母》杂志递给帕姆，想知道她有没有读过那篇关于定期散步重要性的文章。

914
00:42:03.930 --> 00:42:08.710
Yeah, and then she invites Pam to go on twice daily walks with her.
没错，然后她邀请帕姆每天和她一起散步两次。

915
00:42:09.250 --> 00:42:11.590
Jim's like, hey, look who got a walking buddy.
吉姆说，嘿，看谁找到了个散步搭子。

916
00:42:12.890 --> 00:42:17.690
I'll have you know, this episode aired five days after my son was born.
我得告诉你们，这一集播出时，我儿子才刚出生五天。

917
00:42:18.310 --> 00:42:19.090
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

918
00:42:19.090 --> 00:42:19.810
How crazy is that?
这太疯狂了吧？

919
00:42:19.810 --> 00:42:20.890
Yeah, so it's crazy.
是啊，真的很疯狂。

920
00:42:21.370 --> 00:42:25.690
Yeah, that's how close to shooting versus when they air.
没错，拍摄时间和播出时间就是这么接近。

921
00:42:25.930 --> 00:42:27.110
It was very quick.
节奏非常快。

922
00:42:27.990 --> 00:42:30.790
Andy has figured out a way to double the sales.
安迪想出了一个让销售额翻倍的办法。

923
00:42:31.050 --> 00:42:33.470
He is going to have an incentive table.
他打算设置一个奖励台。

924
00:42:33.690 --> 00:42:40.910
He brings everyone in the conference room and he shows them all these things that they can get, you know, as they earn points with their sales.
他把大家叫进会议室，展示了他们通过销售积分可以换取的所有东西。

925
00:42:41.470 --> 00:42:44.530
There's a polar bear stuffed animal, a raccoon stuffed animal.
有一个北极熊毛绒玩具，一个浣熊毛绒玩具。

926
00:42:44.810 --> 00:42:45.990
Sam, I thought of you.
萨姆，我想到你了。

927
00:42:46.810 --> 00:42:59.930
There was a frog stuffed animal, the collective works of John Irving, a Brookstone, looks like mini binoculars, a zippy, small personal desk fan, maternity shirt, tablecloth,
还有一个青蛙毛绒玩具、约翰·欧文的作品集、一个布鲁克斯通的迷你双筒望远镜、一个小巧的个人桌面风扇、一件孕妇衫、一块桌布，

928
00:43:00.130 --> 00:43:01.070
a curling iron.
还有一个卷发棒。

929
00:43:01.070 --> 00:43:02.390
I went to the script.
我查了剧本。

930
00:43:02.590 --> 00:43:04.930
I was like, did it list off what all was on this table?
我在想，剧本里有没有列出桌上所有的东西？

931
00:43:05.230 --> 00:43:05.650
No.
没有。

932
00:43:06.030 --> 00:43:13.150
All it said was, Andy removes the blanket, revealing a bunch of stuffed animals and sharper image type crap.
剧本里只写了：安迪掀开毯子，露出一堆毛绒玩具和类似Sharper Image那种破烂玩意儿。

933
00:43:15.770 --> 00:43:16.890
That's very funny.
那太搞笑了。

934
00:43:17.670 --> 00:43:22.810
Well, the face that Ryan makes in response to the John Irving collection was not scripted.
瑞安看到约翰·欧文作品集时的表情并不是剧本里写的。

935
00:43:23.390 --> 00:43:30.630
And, you know, one of the items that was scripted was the vibrator for 20 points.
而且，你知道，剧本里写的一件物品是价值20分的振动器。

936
00:43:31.450 --> 00:43:33.250
Meredith wants to know, how do you get a point?
梅雷迪思问，怎么才能得到积分？

937
00:43:33.450 --> 00:43:34.690
I loved that delivery.
我太喜欢那句台词的演绎了。

938
00:43:35.490 --> 00:43:37.630
Phil Shea made that vibrator.
那个振动器是菲尔·谢做的。

939
00:43:38.210 --> 00:43:38.650
What?
什么？

940
00:43:39.090 --> 00:43:39.610
Yeah.
是的。

941
00:43:40.030 --> 00:43:40.610
He made it.
是他做的。

942
00:43:40.610 --> 00:43:42.430
Is it like a back massager or something?
那是背部按摩器之类的东西吗？

943
00:43:43.170 --> 00:43:43.990
I'm not sure.
我不确定。

944
00:43:44.210 --> 00:43:47.010
So I did get to talk to Steve Burgess about this episode.
所以我找机会和史蒂夫·伯吉斯聊了聊这一集。

945
00:43:47.210 --> 00:43:49.670
I had a lot of standards and practices questions.
我当时有很多关于审查标准的问题。

946
00:43:50.130 --> 00:43:53.790
And like Randy Cordray, he saved all his emails.
就像兰迪·科德雷一样，他保存了所有的邮件。

947
00:43:53.790 --> 00:43:55.290
So he delivered.
所以他给出了答案。

948
00:43:55.690 --> 00:44:02.630
The big thing with this scene was that we could not show any logos for any real products.
这一幕最大的问题在于，我们不能展示任何真实产品的商标。

949
00:44:02.630 --> 00:44:07.090
So everything that is on that table had to be created by Phil Shea.
所以桌上所有的东西都必须由菲尔·谢制作。

950
00:44:07.330 --> 00:44:11.530
So Phil had to create the vibrator and the packaging.
因此，菲尔不得不亲自制作那个振动器及其包装。

951
00:44:12.710 --> 00:44:18.530
Standards and practices said, quote, we trust any visuals of the vibrator will be staged off
审查部门说，引用原话，我们相信任何关于振动器的画面都会在

952
00:44:18.530 --> 00:44:18.990
camera.
镜头外进行处理。

953
00:44:19.450 --> 00:44:22.290
Well, standards and practices, I have news for you.
好吧，审查部门，我有个消息要告诉你们。

954
00:44:22.670 --> 00:44:24.390
It's very clearly on the table.
它非常清楚地摆在桌子上。

955
00:44:24.650 --> 00:44:25.770
It's on the far left.
就在最左边。

956
00:44:26.270 --> 00:44:26.750
Yeah.
没错。

957
00:44:27.030 --> 00:44:29.830
No one is really excited about any of these prizes.
没人对这些奖品真正感到兴奋。

958
00:44:30.110 --> 00:44:32.770
So Andy is trying to get them more excited.
所以安迪正试图让他们更兴奋一点。

959
00:44:32.910 --> 00:44:33.970
What else can he offer them?
他还能提供什么呢？

960
00:44:34.170 --> 00:44:35.830
How about for 500 points?
五百分怎么样？

961
00:44:35.990 --> 00:44:37.050
I wear a dress to work.
我穿裙子去上班。

962
00:44:37.190 --> 00:44:38.470
This gets a little chuckle.
这引起了一阵轻笑。

963
00:44:38.810 --> 00:44:39.770
Andy is encouraged.
安迪受到了鼓舞。

964
00:44:39.990 --> 00:44:41.750
He really leans into this now.
他现在真的投入进去了。

965
00:44:42.210 --> 00:44:43.450
Jim's going to egg him on.
吉姆打算怂恿他。

966
00:44:43.590 --> 00:44:45.130
He's going to say, what about a thousand points?
他会说，那一千分呢？

967
00:44:45.430 --> 00:44:50.290
Andy said, I will run through the parking lot naked with a donut on my ding dong.
安迪说，我会光着身子跑过停车场，丁丁上套个甜甜圈。

968
00:44:50.290 --> 00:44:51.410
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

969
00:44:51.610 --> 00:44:53.570
Now everyone's really chuckling.
现在大家真的都在笑了。

970
00:44:53.830 --> 00:44:55.710
And Andy's like, oh, yeah, you like that?
安迪心想，哦，是啊，你们喜欢这个？

971
00:44:55.890 --> 00:45:02.470
For 5,000 points, you can tattoo anything you want on the stern of the old SS Bernard.
五千分的话，你们可以在老伯纳德号的船尾纹上任何你们想要的东西。

972
00:45:03.230 --> 00:45:04.370
People go crazy.
人们都疯了。

973
00:45:04.610 --> 00:45:05.070
There's hooting.
有人在起哄。

974
00:45:05.290 --> 00:45:05.810
There's clapping.
有人在鼓掌。

975
00:45:06.730 --> 00:45:06.950
Yes.
是的。

976
00:45:07.310 --> 00:45:09.050
And Jim is like, oh, hold up.
然后吉姆说，哦，等等。

977
00:45:09.090 --> 00:45:10.690
And we can pull our points.
我们可以凑积分。

978
00:45:10.930 --> 00:45:12.070
And Andy's like, yeah.
安迪说，好啊。

979
00:45:12.830 --> 00:45:15.010
Andy, Andy, Andy.
安迪，安迪，安迪。

980
00:45:15.530 --> 00:45:16.130
Yeah.
没错。

981
00:45:16.130 --> 00:45:20.090
Well, they get there really quickly to the 5,000 points.
好吧，他们很快就凑到了五千分。

982
00:45:20.270 --> 00:45:24.330
I think we should take a break because when we get back, the office is a buzz.
我想我们该休息一下，因为回来之后，办公室里一片沸腾。

983
00:45:24.510 --> 00:45:25.870
A buzz for sure.
确实沸腾了。

984
00:45:26.210 --> 00:45:36.250
We are back.
我们回来了。

985
00:45:36.650 --> 00:45:40.310
Everybody is just on their game right now.
每个人现在都干劲十足。

986
00:45:40.510 --> 00:45:43.350
People are answering calls, shouting out stuff.
人们在接电话，大声喊着什么。

987
00:45:43.730 --> 00:45:45.550
Papers are being passed around.
文件在四处传递。

988
00:45:46.210 --> 00:45:51.930
So much activity, especially for Dunder Mifflin, when people are mostly at their desks playing solitaire.
活动量太大了，尤其是对邓德·米夫林来说，平时大家大多坐在桌前玩纸牌游戏。

989
00:45:52.510 --> 00:45:58.770
We got a fan question from Leah K in Arkansas who said, were there specific directions in
我们收到了来自阿肯色州利亚·K的粉丝提问，她说，剧本里是否有具体说明

990
00:45:58.770 --> 00:46:02.650
the script about what each character should be doing when the bullpen is suddenly working
当办公区突然为了达到那五千分而努力工作时，

991
00:46:02.650 --> 00:46:04.730
hard to reach those 5,000 points?
每个角色应该做什么？

992
00:46:05.030 --> 00:46:09.670
It feels like some of the characters are just pretending to do work that they wouldn't actually
感觉有些角色只是在假装做他们平时根本不会做的工作，

993
00:46:09.670 --> 00:46:14.070
do, specifically Kevin, who is frantically punching numbers into a calculator.
特别是凯文，他正疯狂地在计算器上按数字。

994
00:46:14.290 --> 00:46:15.410
Kevin, what are you doing?
凯文，你在干什么？

995
00:46:15.630 --> 00:46:17.010
I love the chaos.
我喜欢这种混乱。

996
00:46:17.170 --> 00:46:18.610
Was it scripted?
这是剧本写的吗？

997
00:46:18.610 --> 00:46:24.990
Well, Leah, the Kevin portion of this activity was scripted, that he was frantically just
嗯，利亚，凯文在这场活动中的表现是剧本写的，他就是疯狂地

998
00:46:24.990 --> 00:46:27.010
typing random numbers into a calculator.
在计算器上乱按数字。

999
00:46:27.250 --> 00:46:30.390
I have it if you want to hear what it said in the shooting draft for Kevin.
如果你想听听拍摄剧本里关于凯文的部分是怎么写的，我这儿有。

1000
00:46:30.530 --> 00:46:31.230
Oh, please do.
哦，请务必读一下。

1001
00:46:31.410 --> 00:46:33.270
Because I was actually really curious, too.
因为其实我也真的很好奇。

1002
00:46:33.530 --> 00:46:34.790
This is what it says.
上面是这么写的。

1003
00:46:35.030 --> 00:46:40.690
Andy strolls through the office towards accounting and sees Kevin is adding like a madman,
安迪溜达着穿过办公室走向会计部，看到凯文像个疯子一样在算账，

1004
00:46:41.030 --> 00:46:43.190
two adding machines at once.
同时用两台加法机。

1005
00:46:43.470 --> 00:46:45.230
Andy says, what are you doing?
安迪问，你在干什么？

1006
00:46:45.850 --> 00:46:47.710
Kevin says, don't talk to me.
凯文说，别跟我说话。

1007
00:46:48.210 --> 00:46:49.770
Andy walks back towards his office.
安迪走回了自己的办公室。

1008
00:46:50.030 --> 00:46:53.930
Oscar says, this didn't make it into the episode, but it's in the shooting draft.
奥斯卡说，这一段没剪进正片里，但剧本初稿里有。

1009
00:46:54.370 --> 00:46:56.330
Oscar says, what are you doing?
奥斯卡问，你在干什么？

1010
00:46:56.550 --> 00:46:58.770
And Kevin says, making numbers.
凯文说，在搞数字。

1011
00:47:02.170 --> 00:47:04.390
Yes, that part was all scripted.
没错，那部分全是照着剧本演的。

1012
00:47:04.510 --> 00:47:06.850
But Leah, the rest of the hustle and bustle was not scripted.
但是莉亚，剩下的那些忙忙碌碌的场景可没写在剧本里。

1013
00:47:06.970 --> 00:47:09.950
It was planned and choreographed by Charles McDougal on the day.
那是查尔斯·麦克道格当天计划并编排好的。

1014
00:47:10.450 --> 00:47:14.990
And, you know, something about Charles that was so great was he was a big fan of movement
你知道，查尔斯最棒的一点就是他非常喜欢在剧集中加入

1015
00:47:14.990 --> 00:47:15.890
in episodes.
走动。

1016
00:47:16.130 --> 00:47:19.530
If you watch any of his episodes, you're going to see more crosses.
如果你看他导演的任何一集，你会发现更多的人员穿梭。

1017
00:47:19.890 --> 00:47:23.350
You're going to see more kind of like background hubbub.
你会看到更多背景里的嘈杂声。

1018
00:47:23.530 --> 00:47:27.190
He was not a fan of us just sitting at our desks playing solitaire.
他不喜欢我们只是坐在办公桌前玩纸牌游戏。

1019
00:47:27.670 --> 00:47:28.510
Not at all.
一点也不喜欢。

1020
00:47:28.630 --> 00:47:29.750
You know, he was action.
你知道，他追求的是动作感。

1021
00:47:30.390 --> 00:47:31.110
That's right.
没错。

1022
00:47:31.650 --> 00:47:35.410
I noticed something as I was passing so many papers.
我在递交那么多文件时注意到了一件事。

1023
00:47:35.630 --> 00:47:38.690
Angela Martin, the accountant, so many papers passing back and forth.
会计安吉拉·马丁，有那么多文件传来传去。

1024
00:47:38.690 --> 00:47:43.650
Pam is like, Angela, I am waddling around the office.
帕姆说，安吉拉，我在办公室里摇摇晃晃地走着。

1025
00:47:44.290 --> 00:47:47.470
There's no other way to describe it except a waddle.
除了摇摇晃晃，没法用别的词来形容。

1026
00:47:47.690 --> 00:47:51.010
And it is because I probably had a front and back wedgie.
那是因为我当时可能前后都卡裆了。

1027
00:47:51.270 --> 00:47:53.770
I didn't even walk like that when I was actually pregnant.
我怀孕的时候走路都没那样。

1028
00:47:53.770 --> 00:47:55.530
But this is the fake pregger belly.
但这可是假孕肚。

1029
00:47:55.810 --> 00:47:57.970
This is the wedgie that you told me about.
这就是你跟我说过的卡裆。

1030
00:47:58.150 --> 00:48:00.890
And with each step I took, it went more up my butt.
我每走一步，它就往我屁股里陷得更深。

1031
00:48:01.530 --> 00:48:03.450
You are describing it accurately.
你描述得很准确。

1032
00:48:03.890 --> 00:48:06.810
That is the experience of wearing a fake pregger belly.
这就是戴着假孕肚的真实体验。

1033
00:48:07.250 --> 00:48:11.870
Yeah, put on a leotard and then put a giant pillow in it and see if you don't get a wedgie.
是啊，穿上一件紧身连衣裤，再塞个大枕头进去，看你会不会卡裆。

1034
00:48:12.670 --> 00:48:14.110
Andy is starting to panic.
安迪开始慌了。

1035
00:48:14.430 --> 00:48:17.510
He is seeing them getting closer and closer to the goal.
他看着他们离目标越来越近。

1036
00:48:17.630 --> 00:48:23.090
There's a whole drawing of like the backside of a man and they're coloring it in red, like
画板上画着一个男人的背影，他们正用红色把它涂满，就像

1037
00:48:23.090 --> 00:48:25.670
heading towards the butt as they get more and more points.
随着得分越来越多，红色正向屁股蔓延。

1038
00:48:26.350 --> 00:48:28.850
He calls his business professor in a panic.
他惊慌失措地给他的商学院教授打电话。

1039
00:48:29.010 --> 00:48:33.050
He wants to know, how do you de-incentivize your employees?
他想知道，该如何消除员工的积极性？

1040
00:48:33.050 --> 00:48:35.990
And he does not get any of the answers he wants.
但他得到的答案都不是他想要的。

1041
00:48:36.430 --> 00:48:39.870
Then we would have cut to this random Dwight scene.
然后我们本该切到这个随机的德怀特场景。

1042
00:48:40.050 --> 00:48:43.630
Remember how I said this episode was full of some random Dwight moments?
还记得我说过这一集里有很多随机的德怀特时刻吗？

1043
00:48:44.190 --> 00:48:44.490
Yes.
记得。

1044
00:48:44.690 --> 00:48:46.250
In the shooting draft, it's in the scene.
在剧本初稿里，这一幕是在正片里的。

1045
00:48:46.370 --> 00:48:47.890
It's also in deleted scenes.
它也被收录在删减片段里。

1046
00:48:48.310 --> 00:48:53.250
Dwight is sitting alone in the corner of the break room as Daryl comes into the vending machines.
德怀特独自坐在休息室的角落里，这时达里尔走过来买零食。

1047
00:48:53.510 --> 00:48:57.670
And Dwight just for no reason decides to narrate the whole moment.
德怀特莫名其妙地决定把这一刻全程解说出来。

1048
00:48:58.030 --> 00:48:59.450
Daryl doesn't say a word.
达里尔一句话也没说。

1049
00:48:59.770 --> 00:49:01.150
I thought you should hear it.
我觉得你应该听听这个。

1050
00:49:02.610 --> 00:49:03.490
There he is.
他就在那儿。

1051
00:49:03.630 --> 00:49:04.210
Snack man.
零食侠。

1052
00:49:04.870 --> 00:49:05.590
Snack attack.
零食突袭。

1053
00:49:06.750 --> 00:49:08.210
Perfect day for a snack.
吃零食的完美一天。

1054
00:49:08.430 --> 00:49:09.590
After a day like yours.
在你经历了这样的一天之后。

1055
00:49:10.250 --> 00:49:11.450
Perfect cheat day, right?
完美的放纵日，对吧？

1056
00:49:12.550 --> 00:49:13.510
What will it be?
选什么呢？

1057
00:49:13.610 --> 00:49:13.930
Chips?
薯片？

1058
00:49:14.070 --> 00:49:14.330
Candy?
糖果？

1059
00:49:14.530 --> 00:49:15.070
Giant cookie?
巨型曲奇？

1060
00:49:15.230 --> 00:49:15.970
Followed by a soda?
再来瓶汽水？

1061
00:49:16.090 --> 00:49:16.550
Who knows?
谁知道呢？

1062
00:49:17.370 --> 00:49:18.450
Decision has been made.
决定已经做好了。

1063
00:49:19.210 --> 00:49:19.670
A chunk.
咔哒一声。

1064
00:49:19.930 --> 00:49:20.650
It falls.
它掉下来了。

1065
00:49:21.250 --> 00:49:23.110
Just like the food falls into your stomach.
就像食物掉进你的胃里一样。

1066
00:49:23.690 --> 00:49:24.990
Have you always worn a belt?
你一直都系着腰带吗？

1067
00:49:25.430 --> 00:49:26.270
Talk to you later.
回头再聊。

1068
00:49:30.320 --> 00:49:32.080
What is happening with Dwight?
德怀特是怎么回事？

1069
00:49:33.440 --> 00:49:34.780
Is he so bored?
他有那么无聊吗？

1070
00:49:35.480 --> 00:49:36.540
I'm going to say something.
我要去说点什么。

1071
00:49:36.980 --> 00:49:37.060
Okay.
好吧。

1072
00:49:37.120 --> 00:49:37.380
Well, yes.
嗯，是的。

1073
00:49:37.460 --> 00:49:38.280
He's checked out.
他完全不在状态。

1074
